The code in this folder is ported from Space-Wrecked, RCJLabs's own game:
the space-wrecked repository at commit a2b4f62d2ecb3049cca8f5b55dbbdc43ede2f2e6
(2026-10-16). It is used here with its owner's permission (decision D86 in
docs/decisions.md). It is not covered by the engine's licence, and may not be
copied, changed or shared apart from this repository without RCJLabs's
permission.

Only this folder is the port. stages/battle.ts and stages/deck/, which read
the deck's tilemap and walkers and hand them to the board, were written for
the engine.

What was ported, from the repository's src/ unless said:
- core/rng.js, whole.
- sim/grid.js, sim/mapText.js and sim/cover.js, whole.
- sim/mapFromShip.js: the map's shape, MARGIN, WRECKS, wallAt and edgeKey.
- sim/terrain.js: tileRule and edgeAt, which cover.js reads.
- sim/gen/site.js: regions().
- tools/battle-map.js (the repository's tools/): renderMap and parseMap.
- render/: battleView.js, battleScene.js, units.js, orbit.js, painter.js,
  solid.js, palette.js, layer.js, frameBudget.js, starfield.js, and
  shipView.js's drawSpace.
- render/figures/: every file.
- data/content.ts: the values the board reads from data/modules.json (the
  tiles legend), data/jobs.json (each job's look and weapon) and
  data/weapons.json (each weapon's held shape), copied as they stand.

The changes:
- Files renamed to the stage's naming: lowercase words joined by hyphens
  (battleView.js is render/battle-view.ts, mapFromShip.js is
  sim/map-from-ship.ts), and imported by those names.
- JavaScript given the types TypeScript needs: interfaces for the map, faces,
  glows, cameras and figures, and casts where a value can't be missing.
  Space-Wrecked's layout is kept, so each file reads line for line against its
  source: each opens with a line telling the engine's formatter to leave it,
  and the fittings' unused parameter g is named _g, as the engine's linter asks.
- document.createElement('canvas') changed to new OffscreenCanvas, in layer.js's
  paintLayer, figures/sprites.js's defaultCanvas and starfield.js's
  paintBackdrop: a stage draws in a worker, which has no document.
- window.devicePixelRatio changed to the frame's: the board reads the pixel
  ratio from the context's transform, which the stage's runner sets to the
  frame's. canvas.js, which read window.devicePixelRatio, is not ported.
- performance.now() changed to a clock that stands still (frame-budget.ts's
  STILL_CLOCK), in frameBudget.js and figures/sprites.js: a stage may read no
  clock but its frame's, which doesn't move during a frame. So every frame is
  a full one, every figure is drawn when first needed, and the page drops the
  frames a slow stage can't keep up with.
- The ship's exterior, which the board doesn't draw, left out: shipView.js keeps
  only drawSpace; exterior.js, hull.js, hullShape.js, pieces.js, props.js,
  shipScene.js, mesh.js, blueprintStyles.js and the builder's sim are not
  ported. solid.js leaves out solidCylinder, solidTube and placeFaces, and
  painter.js the blueprint's batchModel and paintBatches and the builder's
  paintLabels, which only the outside and the builder use.
- palette.js leaves out applyCssVars, which sets CSS on the page, and the
  colony's grounds and buildings and the portraits' colors, which the board
  never draws. Its skins are made from a yard object first, to name their type.
- parseMap gives each area the walls and doors close off a room of its own by
  site.js's regions(), so its floor takes its own tint, where Space-Wrecked's
  puts every tile in room 1; each hatch takes its tile's room. regions() leaves
  space and the hull out of every room, as parseMap did, as well as rock.
